// Function Body:
fn resolve_web_search_mode(
    config_toml: &ConfigToml,
    config_profile: &ConfigProfile,
    features: &Features,
) -> Option<WebSearchMode> 
{
    let web_search_mode_from_config = config_toml.web_search.clone();
    let web_search_mode_from_profile = config_profile.web_search.clone();
    let web_search_mode_from_feature = if features.enabled.contains(&Feature::WebSearchRequest) {
        Some(WebSearchMode::Live)
    } else if features.enabled.contains(&Feature::WebSearchCached) {
        Some(WebSearchMode::Cached)
    } else {
        None
    };

    web_search_mode_from_config.or(web_search_mode_from_profile).or(web_search_mode_from_feature)
}
```

This function firstly clones the `web_search` option from `config_toml` and `config_profile`. Then, it checks if the `WebSearchRequest` or `WebSearchCached` feature is enabled in `features` and sets the corresponding web search mode.

Finally, the function returns the first non-None value from `web_search_mode_from_config`, `web_search_mode_from_profile`, and `web_search_mode_from_feature`.

